## 3. Code conventions

- **TypeScript strict mode** across all apps. No `any` unless wrapping
  third-party untyped APIs.
- **Bun first** for ai-service / cloud / capture-agent. **Vite** for desktop.
- **Hono routes** in ai-service live in `apps/ai-service/src/http/server.ts`
  with auth via `Authorization: Bearer <HTTP_AUTH_TOKEN>`.
- **SQLite + sqlite-vec** for ai-service memory. Schema migrations are
  idempotent additive — see `apps/ai-service/src/context-store/db.ts`
  (currently at v7, recording_sessions added FR92).
- **No mocking the database in tests.** Use real sqlite in-memory; mock-vs-prod
  divergence has burned us.
- **No silent fallbacks.** Throw on bad env, fail-open is OK only where
  explicitly documented (e.g. LLM classifier in procedural pipeline).
- **Default to writing no comments.** Only add one when WHY is non-obvious
  (hidden constraint, subtle invariant, specific bug workaround).
- **Don't add backwards-compatibility hacks.** Renaming unused `_var`,
  re-exporting removed types, `// removed` markers — delete the dead code.

