## 5. Recurring gotchas

- **CF Tunnel + QUIC:** if `https://*.kurdy.uk` returns HTTP 530 while
  containers are up, cloudflared lost QUIC to edge. Fix: `--protocol http2`
  is already set; recreate container if logs spam
  `failed to dial to edge with quic`.
- **Docker Desktop on laptop:** stuck-daemon bug ~every 5 days. Restart via
  `osascript -e 'quit app "Docker Desktop"' && open -a Docker`. Prod on makurdi
  uses Colima — not affected.
- **active-win Accessibility prompt loop:** capture-agent calls with
  `accessibilityPermission: false, screenRecordingPermission: false`. The
  Swift helper is ad-hoc signed, macOS TCC can't durably grant it. App name
  is preserved (works without permission), title/url drop (we OCR them anyway).
- **Multi-origin CORS:** `MINDWTR_CLOUD_CORS_ORIGIN` is comma-separated. Server
  picks the request's Origin if it's in the allowlist (AsyncLocalStorage
  context), else falls back to first allowed. `Vary: Origin` is always set.
- **Bun idleTimeout:** mindwtr-cloud sets `idleTimeout: 120` (was 10s default)
  — required for /v1/data full-blob PUT from mobile on slow uplinks.
- **Web app self-heal:** desktop bundle has origin-aware cloud URL +
  self-heal in `storage-adapter-web.ts`. If a stored URL is for the wrong
  origin (localhost on gtd.kurdy.uk, or API pointed at the web origin
  itself), it rewrites to the correct target on next load.
- **Upstream merge can drop files silently.** Audit recipe in
  `~/.claude/.../memory/project_mindwtr_upstream_merge_lossy.md` (Sergey's
  Claude Code memory) — same loss likely affects other dirs.

## 6. Worktrees

If GTD_automation/CLAUDE.md mentions worktrees — those are for that repo. This
repo doesn't currently use the same worktree workflow; if Sergey asks for a
worktree here, ask first what isolation he needs (Docker compose project name,
ports), since the pattern isn't standardized here yet.

## 7. Testing

- **Vitest** for unit. Tests co-located as `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` next to
  source.
- **Real SQLite** for memory tests, not mocks.
- **Don't bypass the LLM** with stubs unless the test is specifically about
  retry/error paths. Most logic tests should accept "skip if LLM_API_KEY unset".

## 8. When unsure

- Read the file first, state actual current behavior, then propose change.
- For architectural what-ifs, point at the relevant SCP in
  `GTD_automation/_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/sprint-change-proposal-*.md`
  and quote it.
- BMAD is the source of truth for "what is planned". Chat is exploration.
